,"description":"Denial-of-service attack","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21ea9-f885-773e-a342-cf6dd0bcff1b","description":"Dumpster diving","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21ea9-f885-7151-82a7-e45e445afddd","category":"01a21e5d-ee8b-768b-8713-3f779a056aaa","question":"Which attack tries leaked username-password pairs on other services?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"Credential stuffing exploits people reusing passwords across sites.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21ea9-f885-712e-a9ce-abc0b03d8b98","description":"Credential stuffing","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21ea9-f885-7f36-a3ca-2f76f29f7d4b","description":"Password spraying","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21ea9-f885-7b74-8b55-8fb908a13852","description":"Rainbow table cracking","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21ea9-f885-75fc-a09c-f785b8a8248f","description":"Session fixation","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21ea9-f885-7aaa-98fb-12e4d53f0959","category":"01a21e5d-ee8b-768b-8713-3f779a056aaa","question":"Which attack tries a few commonly used login secrets against many accounts?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"Password spraying spreads attempts across accounts to reduce lockouts.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21ea9-f885-78a4-86c2-1cd71543956b","description":"Password spraying","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21ea9-f885-74d3-9a60-985b77f19210","description":"Credential stuffing","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21ea9-f885-7127-9c59-2b1fb6357076","description":"Keystroke logging","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21ea9-f885-7c47-babd-3a7b3e0d588b","description":"ARP spoofing","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21ea9-f885-7290-a79d-5772c9d29bc7","category":"01a21e5d-ee8b-768b-8713-3f779a056aaa","question":"What is random data added to each password before hashing called?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"Unique salts make precomputed attacks and identical-password matching harder.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21ea9-f885-7b45-a302-dd95c01a90f1","description":"Salt","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21ea9-f885-710c-aba7-8658d0a4d31e","description":"Session key","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21ea9-f885-77ef-b8f6-98a2421cb731","description":"Nonce","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21ea9-f885-7bf7-9568-449b6cb58643","description":"Checksum","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21ea9-f885-7356-8795-81a08b66acc5","category":"01a21e5d-ee8b-768b-8713-3f779a056aaa","question":"Which one-way operation maps data of any size to a fixed-size digest?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"A secure hash is designed to be difficult to reverse or forge through collisions.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21ea9-f885-7de1-9b0f-3f6e2133a886","description":"Cryptographic hashing","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21ea9-f885-7f9c-be36-dd68c53f0cb4","description":"Symmetric encryption","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21ea9-f885-7feb-ad91-24b8de6e19ed","description":"Lossless compression","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21ea9-f885-7703-b14a-d1618f02e3db","description":"Digital watermarking","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21ea9-f885-7007-ae6d-b543569a65b6","category":"01a21e5d-ee8b-768b-8713-3f779a056aaa","question":"Which cryptographic method uses the same secret key for encryption and decryption?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"Symmetric encryption is efficient but requires a shared secret.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21ea9-f885-7a8b-9264-a4618224d04e","description":"Symmetric encryption","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21ea9-f885-7a74-8919-f9c9dd704ba3","description":"Public-key encryption","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21ea9-f885-75db-824a-c85941615df6","description":"Hashing","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21ea9-f885-7d57-b8bd-37c26f63930c","description":"Steganography","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21ea9-f885-72cd-aae0-2ef6111a4c4e","category":"01a21e5d-ee8b-768b-8713-3f779a056aaa","question":"In public-key encryption, which key does the recipient use to decrypt a confidential message?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"A message encrypted for a recipient can be decrypted with the matching private key.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21ea9-f885-7026-bc41-1f22e31eccef","description":"Recipient\'s private key","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21ea9-f885-77d4-9902-d3776167093b","description":"Recipient\'s public key","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21ea9-f885-79eb-9a24-f8361a7f0845","description":"Sender\'s private key","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21ea9-f885-7a40-9d91-440deaccfea8","description":"Sender\'s public key","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21ea9-f885-77cd-b3ac-f734b6178f08","category":"01a21e5d-ee8b-768b-8713-3f779a056aaa","question":"Which cryptographic mechanism verifies a message\'s origin and integrity using a signer\'s private key?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"Others use the corresponding public key to verify a digital signature.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21ea9-f885-7adf-8d1f-f080d868c1bc","description":"Digital signature","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21ea9-f885-764b-8a4d-44da1ac2df56","description":"Symmetric block cipher","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21ea9-f885-734b-90b2-bcaa481be062","description":"Hash table","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21ea9-f885-76fe-a192-a74203ab1dea","description":"Data masking","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21ea9-f885-7972-8cfe-229d18f79dba","category":"01a21e5d-ee8b-768b-8713-3f779a056aaa","question":"Which symmetric encryption standard did NIST adopt in 2001 as the successor to DES?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"AES is based on the Rijndael cipher and supports three key sizes.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21ea9-f885-7dce-b6d3-5bcec68c8be3","description":"AES","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21ea9-f885-7f9d-9cd9-d152663b3b0c","description":"RSA","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21ea9-f885-7338-9fd4-78ea9565e292","description":"Triple DES","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21ea9-f885-77c5-b143-9b35cebee76d","description":"SHA-1","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21ea9-f885-70de-b388-10768dd59a31","category":"01a21e5d-ee8b-768b-8713-3f779a056aaa","question":"Which public-key algorithm is named after Rivest, Shamir, and Adleman?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"RSA was publicly described in 1977 and can be used for encryption and signatures.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21ea9-f885-712b-ad27-258989b5f74f","description":"RSA","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21ea9-f885-72cb-b3cd-a8d67e0f0cbb","description":"AES","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21ea9-f885-72e4-8a74-76a912f5036c","description":"DSA","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21ea9-f885-7930-b660-48f9d1d49cc1","description":"ECC","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21ea9-f885-724f-83d7-b7647d486b43","category":"01a21e5d-ee8b-768b-8713-3f779a056aaa","question":"Which method lets two parties establish a shared secret over an insecure channel?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"Diffie-Hellman needs authentication to protect against man-in-the-middle attacks.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21ea9-f886-7b07-84dc-b849b16b7ba6","description":"Diffie-Hellman key exchange","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21ea9-f886-7036-bddc-43a5fb0e8cc7","description":"Caesar cipher","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21ea9-f886-760a-b59f-4cad1d20c116","description":"Huffman coding","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21ea9-f886-7a59-9723-f53425edd188","description":"Merkle tree","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21ea9-f886-7ade-bbed-96071467e51b","category":"01a21e5d-ee8b-768b-8713-3f779a056aaa","question":"Which trusted entity signs the credentials that browsers use to authenticate websites?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"A certificate authority signs certificates that link identities to public keys.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21ea9-f886-70f8-b2cb-169111b82cd5","description":"Certificate authority","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21ea9-f886-7234-966b-fa58893afee6","description":"Domain registrar","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21ea9-f886-77b6-9fcc-a4d0023dd9f0","description":"Internet exchange point","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21ea9-f886-7709-942f-5068d809a8ed","description":"Package maintainer","correct_